{
  "root_cause": "The Pikaday date picker's keyboard handler (_onKeyChange) does not handle the Tab key (keyCode 9). When a user types a date in the bound input field and presses Tab, the picker remains open and its focusable elements (day buttons, navigation buttons) intercept the Tab navigation, preventing focus from moving to the next form field.",
  "repair_strategy": "Add a case for keyCode 9 (Tab) in the _onKeyChange switch statement. When Tab is pressed while the bound input field is focused (e.target === opts.field), hide the picker to release its focus trap and allow the browser's default Tab behavior to move focus to the next form field.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "pikaday.js",
      "sha256": "a50b66482ec18884a7200882e9b523d9192b224b40b296cdd4080530f114fa75",
      "before": "        self._onKeyChange = function(e)
        {
            e = e || window.event;

            if (self.isVisible()) {

                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }
            }
        };",
      "after": "        self._onKeyChange = function(e)
        {
            e = e || window.event;

            if (self.isVisible()) {

                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 9: // Tab
                        if (e.target === opts.field) {
                            self.hide();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }
            }
        };"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Keyboard users can now tab from the date input field to the next form field (guests) after typing a date, satisfying WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) and 2.4.3 (Focus Order).",
  "functional_risks": [
    "Minimal - only affects Tab key behavior when the picker is visible and the input field is focused",
    "Arrow key navigation within the picker remains unchanged",
    "Date selection with Enter/Space still works",
    "Picker closes on Tab from field as intended"
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "Tab from checkin field moves focus to guests field",
    "Arrow keys still navigate dates when picker is open",
    "Date selection with Enter/Space still works",
    "Picker closes on Tab from field"
  ]
}

reasoning:
The user wants me to fix the Pikaday date picker's keyboard handling so that pressing Tab from the date input field moves focus to the next form field (guests). The issue is in the `_onKeyChange` function which doesn't handle the Tab key (keyCode 9).

Looking at the previous attempt, I tried to add a case for keyCode 9 (Tab) but the proposal was rejected because of "maxLength" key errors. Now I need to provide a corrected proposal with the exact same fix but without any invalid keys.

The fix should be in pikaday.js, adding a case for keyCode 9 (Tab) in the `_onKeyChange` switch statement. When Tab is pressed while the bound input field is focused, hide the picker to release its focus trap and allow the browser's default Tab behavior to move focus to the next form field.

Let me look at the current `_onKeyChange` function in the source:

```javascript
self._onKeyChange = function(e)
{
    e = e || window.event;

    if (self.isVisible()) {

        switch(e.keyCode){
            case 13:
            case 27:
                if (opts.field) {
                    opts.field.blur();
                }
                break;
            case 37:
                self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                break;
            case 38:
                self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                break;
            case 39:
                self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                break;
            case 40:
                self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                break;
            case 8:
            case 46:
                self.setDate(null);
                break;
        }
    }
};
```

I need to add a case for keyCode 9 (Tab) before the other cases. The fix should check if the target is the bound field (opts.field) and if so, hide the picker.

